{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-86344",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The area $A$ under the curve $y=v(t)$ can be approximated using the formula\n\n$$\nA≈(\\overset{\\text{heights}}{\\overset{⏞}{v(1)+v(2)+v(3)+v(4)}})\\cdot {{Δt}_{⏟}}_{\\text{width}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we now set up a table with the values of $v(t)$ at each point:\n\n| $t$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $v(t)$ | $18$ | $k$ | $25$ | $27$ |\n\nNow, we obtain the following approximation for the area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈(18+k+25+27)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =70+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in the given context, the area under the curve represents the total distance that the minivan traveled. Since we are given that the right Riemann sum approximation of the total distance is $85$ meters,  we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}70+k & =85 \\\\ k & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
